+
+New render switches (`--set`). The haze, fog and desaturation defaults change nothing for scenes that do not set them
+(the desaturation default is the PBR Neutral constant used before); the ground bounce and subject metering are on by
+default and so change every G2 frame with the analytic sky or auto exposure:
+
+| Switch | Meaning | Env scenes set |
+|---|---|---|
+| `hazelowsun=<x>` | factor on the aerosol haze with the sun on the horizon, easing to 1 by 25 degrees | 0.55 (arid 0.75) |
+| `foghighsun=<x>` | factor on the clear air's height fog with the sun high, from 1 at 15 degrees to x at 45 (mist and rain bring it back towards 1) | 0.15 (arid 0.3) |
+| `bounce=0\|1` | the sky light's lower hemisphere is sunlit ground of the scene's ground albedo | on; biome albedo |
+| `metering=subject\|centre` | auto exposure weights the lower frame and clamps samples 1.5 stops over the mean | subject (default) |
+| `neutraldesat=<0..1>` | how far the tone map's shoulder desaturates highlights (default 0.15) | benchmark scenes 0.08 |
+
