+# G2 stage polish1: the visual critic's first pass, worked most visible first
+
+Stage agent polish1, branch `g2/polish1` (cut from `g2/trunk` f6ea1c1), 2026-11-12. Scope: the eleven ranked issues of
+the visual critic's iteration 1 on the benchmark scenes A–E (`reports/scenes.md`), as many as could be done well, then
+the canonical capture set again and before/after sheets per issue. MonoGame 3D only, presentation only (DR42: nothing
+here reads back into the simulation; the battle trace of scenes C and D is read-only). All numbers below were measured
+in this container on **llvmpipe (Mesa software GL on 4 logical CPUs of an Intel Xeon at 2.10 GHz, 15 GB RAM, shared with
+other sessions; one-minute load average between 1.3 and 9.1 while this stage ran): llvmpipe, not Victus evidence**. No
+hardware GPU ran this code. Quality references were used as references only; nothing player-facing names another game
+(D-069). These are prototype frames, not production art.
+
+**Verdict, honestly.** All eleven issues were worked. Four are done to the extent the critic's note asked (ranks 1, 2,
+3 and 8); seven only partly (4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11), and §1 names what is missing for each. Ten of the eleven change the
+canonical stills visibly; the standards' flutter (rank 8) is small at the canonical framings. The largest steps: the
+meadow (green instead of sand at golden hour, varied instead of flat felt, no hard line where the ground cover ended),
+the land beyond the map (hills, woods and fields instead of a flat hazy plain), the shadow acne (gone in the grazing-sun
+test and the rout and vista shots), the close beats' staging (no crowd soldier between the camera and the officer or the
+commander), the skin (no magenta palms or cheek bands) and the river's bright screen edge (gone). Still placeholder
+(§5): faces at the closest framings, the fallen pile, the far land's woods and settlements, the villages' life, smoke
+structure, rain splashes. None of it is production quality, and none of it says anything about performance on the
+Victus.
+
+## 1. What changed, per issue
+
+Before = the stage-scenes canonical captures (`captures/scenes/g2/`, G2 at f6ea1c1); after = this stage's canonical
+captures (`captures/polish1/`, §2), both 1920 × 1080 with 8 samples. The measured figures come from
